  "content": {
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "order": 1,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s1",
            "text": "In movies, scientists bring back the dinosaurs."
          },
          {
            "id": "s2",
            "text": "They find dinosaur DNA and use it to clone dinosaurs."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "order": 2,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s3",
            "text": "Unfortunately, this is only fiction."
          },
          {
            "id": "s4",
            "text": "Scientists cannot really do this."
          },
          {
            "id": "s5",
            "text": "DNA becomes damaged over time."
          },
          {
            "id": "s6",
            "text": "Dinosaurs went extinct millions of years ago."
          },
          {
            "id": "s7",
            "text": "So, their DNA is too damaged to use."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "order": 3,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s8",
            "text": "However, we could clone other extinct animals."
          },
          {
            "id": "s9",
            "text": "Their DNA is not as old, so it is less damaged."
          },
          {
            "id": "s10",
            "text": "For example, the mammoth went extinct only 10,000 years ago."
          },
          {
            "id": "s11",
            "text": "We might be able to bring it back."
          },
          {
            "id": "s12",
            "text": "Do you want to see a mammoth?"
          },
          {
            "id": "s13",
            "text": "Someday, you just might!"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
